-- NEW CONTENT (Castle population, docs/analysis/castle-population/README.md):
-- templates 174-186 fill World 8 with ambient friendlies and a level 2-4 NID guard
-- spread. The Castle's original SpawnSets were never recovered (spawn_sets.sql and
-- spawn_points.sql are empty), so none of this is ORIGINAL_DATA except the names.
--
-- Names are shipped monikers, never new ids: `name_id` goes onto the AoI create
-- packet raw and the client resolves it against its own PAK string table.
--   7552 DN_Ob_Sc_HumanBody_Cellblock_StasisPrisoner = 'Op-CORE Soldier' (174-176, 180)
--   6964 DN_Castle_Medic_Pvt_1-3                     = 'Castle Medic' (177)
--   7036 DN_npc_int_SgtStanton_Castle                = 'Sgt. Stanton' (178)
--   7342 DN_NPC_MG_Ogilvie_Hebridan_PraxisContact    = 'Ogilvie' (179). The Castle
--        moniker 8895 DN_npc_int_Ogilvie_Castle ships an EMPTY string, so it would
--        render no name; 7342 is the only non-empty plain 'Ogilvie'.
--   7417 DN_Mb_Castle_NID_Guard_St_1-5               = 'NID Guard' (181-183)
--   7703 DN_Mb_Castle_Exterior_NID_Guard_St_1-5      = 'Exterior NID Guard' (184-186)
-- The `_St_1-5` suffix is the moniker's level band, so reusing both guard names at
-- levels 2-4 stays inside the band the strings shipped for.
--
-- Friendlies (174-180) are faction 1, which the Praxis row of the faction
-- reaction table reads as FRIENDLY; no ability set, so they never fight. The
-- escaped Op-CORE prisoners wear the prisoner garb Gerschon (149) and Zuritska (168)
-- wear, plus `AR_Global.Prisoner_Boots`; 174/175/178 carry the SMG they took from
-- the armory. Heads avoid 01 (every NID guard), 05 (Zuritska) and 09 (Gerschon).
-- 175 is 174 with a 3 u wander and a 6-15 s dwell, for the safe Armory only.
-- 176 is unarmed: the stasis-sick and still-caged prisoners (dialog 4982: soldiers
-- "collapsing with seizures", "from the East Wing stasis pods"). 177 is female so
-- the triage group is not four copies of one body. 180 is a prop corpse, class
-- 'being' like template 14 (Cpt. Frost), with the same prisoner-corpse mesh: it is
-- one of Copplemann's fire team ("They didn't make it", dialog 2574). 'being' never
-- AI-ticks, and a static mesh is mandatory for a prop or it renders invisible.
-- Named cameos use the seed's level-50 sentinel for talk-only NPCs; the generic
-- friendlies use level 4, the top of the Castle mission band.
--
-- Hostiles 181-186 are verbatim clones of 148 (inside, SGC gear) and 146 (outside,
-- winter clothes): ability set 3 (559 Automatic Weapon Auto Attack), `use_cover`
-- true, faction 10. Their levels and names are the only change from the old
-- level-1 templates 145/146/148, which keep theirs. Loot (a later owner decision in
-- the same packet, D-CP09): every Castle hostile template now rolls a Castle loot
-- table -- 4 for the rank-and-file guards (146, 148, 181, 182, 184, 185), 5 for the
-- L4 guards and named/officer mobs (183, 186, 169 Romney, 170 Muelbach, 171 Bravo
-- officers) and 6 for the drones (145). See loot.sql for the rows and the rates.
-- What `level` drives on a mob, and nothing else reads it:
--   max HP  = 200 + 50 * level   (cell-world space_manager/spawn.rs), so 300/350/400
--   kill XP = 10 * level         (cell-combat abilities/loot_drop.rs), so 20/30/40
--   the client's onLevelUpdate on the AoI create packet (class 'mob' and 'being').
-- Damage, hit chance, aggro, leash and threat do not read it, so a level-4 guard
-- hits exactly as hard as a level-1 one; the spread only changes how long a guard
-- takes to kill and what it pays.
-- Radii, chosen so neighbouring groups do not chain-pull a whole corridor:
--   aggro_radius 15 inside / 20 outside (runtime default 18). Interior posts sit in
--   corridors where 18 u reaches through a doorway into the next room; the open
--   field gets a longer sight line.
--   assist_radius 12 (default 10). Every group is authored with its members within
--   12 u of a neighbour and at least 12 u from any other group, so shooting one
--   guard rallies its post and nothing else. Assist never chains. The one deliberate
--   exception is the Interrogation Block pair, which stands 5-6 u from Romney (169)
--   as his escort.
